<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/isoAutomationLevel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The level of automation describes a spectrum of system capability, defining\nthe degree of control and decision-making authority a system possesses\nrelative to an external control.\n\nThis classification helps to define the roles and responsibilities of both the\nhuman operator and the automated system. It is a critical component for risk\nassessment, regulatory compliance, and user interface design."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/other> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Any other specialized or custom verification method that fits the context."@en .
